{
  "name": "LEARN — Field Triage Output",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "Captures lessons and error signatures from Field Triage outputs into the Shared Brain.",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": ["**/Field-Triage/**/field_triage_analysis*.md", "**/Field-Triage/**/dev_team_findings*.md", "**/field-triage/**/field_triage_analysis*.md", "**/field-triage/**/dev_team_findings*.md"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "LEARN phase (lightweight) — Field Triage output.\n\nA new Field Triage file has been created. Your job is to check if it contains any knowledge worth saving to the Shared Brain.\n\nRead the newly created file. Look only for the following — do not invent findings:\n- Error signatures or log patterns not already catalogued in pattern_registry.md\n- Connections between this production incident and a gap in existing test coverage\n- Environment-specific failure modes (e.g. behaviour that differs between staging and production)\n\nFor new error signatures:\n1. Open .kiro/memory/products/pos/pattern_registry.md and check if this signature is already documented. If yes, skip.\n2. If genuinely new, append to .kiro/memory/products/pos/pattern_registry.md using this exact format:\n\n### {Error Name}\n  {Exact log line or pattern}\n- Cause: {root cause}\n- Diagnosis: {steps to confirm}\n- Resolution: {fix or workaround}\n- Ticket: {ticket ID}\n\nFor new lessons (not error signatures):\n1. Open .kiro/memory/products/pos/lessons_learned.md and scan for a similar entry. If similar exists, skip.\n2. If genuinely new, append one line using this format:\n   [DATE] [TICKET-ID] [LOGGED] [FIELD] — {concise lesson in one sentence}\n\nRules:\n- Do NOT evaluate any finding for promotion to product.md\n- Do NOT modify project_context.md\n- Do NOT rewrite or edit existing entries\n- If nothing new is found, do nothing and do not write anything"
  }
}
